Description: Do not clear the auth cookie in the answer to a request that sent none
 maybeReverseProxy answered a request without the auth cookie with the
 challenge page and a Set-Cookie that clears the cookie. A browser loads
 subresources of the challenge page (here /favicon.ico, which the site
 redirects to an image) while it solves the challenge. When such a request
 leaves before the pass-challenge answer sets the cookie and its answer
 comes back after it, the clearing Set-Cookie removes the cookie that the
 browser has just received. The next page then passes with the cookie, and
 its stylesheets and scripts get the challenge page instead: the page is
 shown with no style.
 .
 A request that sent no cookie has no cookie to clear, so its answer now
 sets none. A request that sent an invalid, expired or otherwise refused
 cookie still gets it cleared, as before. TestNoClearCookieWithoutCookie
 covers both.
Author: Marcos Mendez <mendez.foto@gmail.com>
Forwarded: no
